<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>BifroSSH package repositories</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 46rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  pre { background: #8882; padding: .75rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 6px; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
</style>
<h1>BifroSSH</h1>
<p>
  Package repositories for <a href="https://github.com/AalmanSadath/BifroSSH">BifroSSH</a>,
  a GUI SSH client with built-in SFTP and keychain management. Currently
  <strong>@VERSION@</strong>. Add one and updates arrive with the rest of your system.
</p>

<h2>Flatpak</h2>
<pre><code>flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists flathub https://dl.flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists bifrossh @BASE@/bifrossh.flatpakrepo
flatpak install bifrossh @APP_ID@</code></pre>

<h2>Debian, Ubuntu</h2>
<pre><code>curl -fsSL @BASE@/bifrossh.sources | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/bifrossh.sources
sudo apt update
sudo apt install bifrossh</code></pre>

<h2>Fedora, RHEL</h2>
<pre><code>sudo dnf config-manager addrepo --from-repofile=@BASE@/bifrossh.repo
sudo dnf install bifrossh</code></pre>
<p>On dnf 4 (RHEL 9 and older Fedora) the first line is
<code>sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo @BASE@/bifrossh.repo</code>.</p>

<h2>Going back a version</h2>
<p>The last few releases stay available.</p>
<pre><code># Flatpak: list them, then pick one
flatpak remote-info --log bifrossh @APP_ID@
flatpak update --commit=COMMIT @APP_ID@

# apt
apt list -a bifrossh
sudo apt install bifrossh=VERSION

# dnf
sudo dnf downgrade bifrossh</code></pre>

<p>Everything here is signed with the key at <a href="@BASE@/bifrossh.asc">bifrossh.asc</a>.</p>
